---
import { approaches, interview, segments, phases } from '../../data/dedc02CodingLesson';
const { part = 'approaches' } = Astro.props as { part?: 'approaches' | 'practice' };
const creatorExample = 'https://www.thedegreedoctor.com/blog/braun-and-clarke-thematic-analysis-how-to-do-the-six-step-process-in-your-qualitative-research-project';
const codingGuide = 'https://gradcoach.com/inductive-deductive-coding/';
const abductionSource = 'https://doi.org/10.1177/0735275112457914';
---
{part === 'approaches' && <section class="slide" data-title="Inductive, deductive and abductive coding" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
  <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Coding approaches · question → reason → compare</span></header>
  {(['en','zh'] as const).map((language) => <div data-language={language} hidden={language === 'zh'} lang={language === 'zh' ? 'zh-Hant' : 'en'}>
    <h2>{language === 'zh' ? '代碼與解釋從哪裡來？' : 'Where do codes and explanations come from?'}</h2>
    <p>{language === 'zh' ? '先討論各問題，再展開比較分析邏輯。這些邏輯可用於不同質性方法。' : 'Discuss each question before opening the explanation. These logics can inform different qualitative methods.'}</p>
    <div class="qa-coding-grid">{approaches.map((approach) => <article><h3>{approach[language].name}</h3><p class="qa-coding-route">{approach[language].route}</p><p>{approach[language].question}</p><details class="qa-reveal"><summary>{language === 'zh' ? '比較分析邏輯' : 'Compare the logic'}</summary><p>{approach[language].explanation}</p><p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '檢查：' : 'Check: '}</strong>{approach[language].check}</p></details></article>)}</div>
    <p class="qa-note">{language === 'zh' ? '混合編碼結合資料與既有概念的代碼來源。溯因推理還須指出令人意外的觀察、比較可能解釋，並尋找進一步證據。' : 'Hybrid coding combines data-led and prior-concept codes. Abductive reasoning also identifies a puzzle, compares possible explanations and seeks further evidence.'}</p>
    <p class="qa-source"><a href={codingGuide} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{language === 'zh' ? '編碼取向參考' : 'Coding approaches reference'} ↗</a> · <a href={abductionSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Timmermans &amp; Tavory (2012) ↗</a></p>
  </div>)}
</div></section>}
{part === 'practice' && <section class="slide" data-title="Final practice · interview transcript" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
  <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 6 · final practice · read and code</span></header>
  {(['en','zh'] as const).map((language) => <div data-language={language} hidden={language === 'zh'} lang={language === 'zh' ? 'zh-Hant' : 'en'}>
    <h2>{language === 'zh' ? '最後練習：閱讀訪談並編碼' : 'Final practice: read and code the interview'}</h2>
    <p class="qa-question"><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '課堂問題：' : 'Classroom question: '}</strong>{language === 'zh' ? '疫情期間在家工作如何改變日常工作生活？' : 'How did working at home during the pandemic reshape everyday working life?'}</p>
    <div class="qa-interview"><p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '訪談者：' : 'Interviewer: '}</strong>{interview[language].question}</p><p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '參與者：' : 'Participant:'}</strong></p>{interview[language].paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}</div>
    <p class="qa-teacher">{language === 'zh' ? '標記每個有意義的片語或句子。哪個標籤貼近資料？哪個位置可能需要多於一個代碼？保留完整敘述作語境。' : 'Mark each meaningful phrase or sentence. Which label stays close to the material? Where might a segment need more than one code? Keep the full account as context.'}</p>
  </div>)}
</div></section>}
{part === 'practice' && <section class="slide" data-title="Final practice · compare coding routes" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
  <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 6 · final practice · compare coding routes</span></header>
  {(['en','zh'] as const).map((language) => <div data-language={language} hidden={language === 'zh'} lang={language === 'zh' ? 'zh-Hant' : 'en'}>
    <h2>{language === 'zh' ? '同一段資料，三條分析路徑' : 'One passage, three analytic routes'}</h2>
    <p>{language === 'zh' ? '你的代碼由文本還是既有概念出發？靈活安排與難以停止工作同時存在，會提出甚麼疑問？' : 'Do your codes begin with the text or prior concepts? What puzzle arises when flexibility and difficulty stopping work coexist?'}</p>
    <details class="qa-reveal"><summary>{language === 'zh' ? '1 · 比較歸納與演繹編碼' : '1 · Compare inductive and deductive coding'}</summary>
      <p>{language === 'zh' ? '演繹欄使用教師為示範預先設定的工作生活框架；各格界定該代碼的適用範圍。兩欄皆為本課對訪談的分析示例。' : 'The deductive column uses an instructor-defined work-life framework set before this demonstration; each cell defines the code’s scope. Both columns illustrate analysis of the interview.'}</p>
      <div class="qa-table-wrap"><table class="qa-coding-table"><thead><tr><th>{language === 'zh' ? '訪談原句' : 'Interview phrase'}</th><th>{language === 'zh' ? '歸納：由文本建立的標籤' : 'Inductive: text-led label'}</th><th>{language === 'zh' ? '演繹：起始代碼及定義' : 'Deductive: starting code and definition'}</th></tr></thead><tbody>{segments.map((segment) => <tr><th scope="row">“{segment[language]}”</th><td>{language === 'zh' ? segment.codeZh : segment.codeEn}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? segment.deductiveZh : segment.deductiveEn}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    </details>
    <details class="qa-reveal"><summary>{language === 'zh' ? '2 · 溯因：解釋疑問並比較替代解釋' : '2 · Abduction: explain the puzzle and compare alternatives'}</summary>
      <p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '疑問：' : 'Puzzle: '}</strong>{language === 'zh' ? '參與者重視「靈活安排及無須通勤」，卻感到「一直處於工作狀態」。' : 'The participant values “the flexibility and lack of commute” while feeling “always on the clock”.'}</p>
      <p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '可能解釋：' : 'Possible explanation: '}</strong>{language === 'zh' ? '選擇工作地點與控制何時停止工作可能是兩回事。' : 'Control over work location may differ from control over when work ends.'}</p>
      <p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '替代解釋：' : 'Alternative: '}</strong>{language === 'zh' ? '困難可能與疫情的暫時安排或組織回覆期望有關。' : 'The difficulty may reflect temporary pandemic arrangements or organisational expectations about responding.'}</p>
      <p><strong>{language === 'zh' ? '下一步證據：' : 'Next evidence: '}</strong>{language === 'zh' ? '比較工作時間期望不同的人及不同時期的敘述；尋找能區分各解釋的資料。' : 'Compare accounts with different working-hour expectations and at different times; seek material that distinguishes the explanations.'}</p>
    </details>
    <p class="qa-source">{language === 'zh' ? '教學延伸：演繹框架及溯因解釋由本課加入。溯因方法依據：' : 'Teaching extensions: the deductive framework and abductive explanations are added for this lesson. Abductive reasoning: '}<a href={abductionSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Timmermans &amp; Tavory (2012) ↗</a></p>
  </div>)}
</div></section>}
{part === 'practice' && <section class="slide" data-title="Final practice · six analytic phases" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
  <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 6 · final practice · six analytic phases</span></header>
  {(['en','zh'] as const).map((language) => <div data-language={language} hidden={language === 'zh'} lang={language === 'zh' ? 'zh-Hant' : 'en'}>
    <h2>{language === 'zh' ? '從初始代碼走向分析敘述' : 'From initial codes to an analytic account'}</h2>
    <p>{language === 'zh' ? '以這份遙距工作訪談，練習Braun與Clarke的六階段。各卡先問問題，再揭示本課示例。分析會反覆往返各階段。' : 'Practise Braun and Clarke’s six phases with the remote-work interview. Discuss each question, then reveal the lesson illustration. Revisit earlier phases as your interpretation develops.'}</p>
    <div class="qa-remote-phases">{phases.map((phase,index) => <article><h3>{index+1} · {phase[language].name}</h3><p>{phase[language].question}</p><details class="qa-reveal"><summary>{language === 'zh' ? '比較本課示例' : 'Compare the lesson illustration'}</summary><p>{phase[language].output}</p></details></article>)}</div>
    <p class="qa-note">{language === 'zh' ? '一份訪談可用來練習編碼與詮釋。跨資料的主題需要更完整證據；本頁概念與段落皆屬暫定教學示例。' : 'One interview supports practice in coding and interpretation. Dataset-wide themes require fuller evidence; the ideas and paragraph here remain provisional teaching illustrations.'}</p>
    <p class="qa-source"><a href={creatorExample} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{language === 'zh' ? 'Elizabeth Yardley · 六階段教學' : 'Elizabeth Yardley · six-phase guide'} ↗</a> · <a href="https://doi.org/10.1191/1478088706qp063oa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Braun &amp; Clarke (2006) ↗</a></p>
  </div>)}
</div></section>}

{part === 'practice' && <section class="slide" data-title="Coding terminology across methods" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide-inner">
  <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Coding terminology · traditions, purposes and procedures</span></header>
  {(['en','zh'] as const).map((language) => <div data-language={language} hidden={language === 'zh'} lang={language === 'zh' ? 'zh-Hant' : 'en'}>
    <h2>{language === 'zh' ? '編碼術語隨方法與傳統而變' : 'Coding terminology follows the method'}</h2>
    <p class="qa-note">{language === 'zh' ? '質性分析沒有一套通用的「三級編碼」要求。下表比較紮根理論各傳統的編碼階段；主題分析、內容分析、敘事分析及論述分析各有自己的分析程序。' : 'Qualitative analysis has no universal requirement for “three-level coding”. The table compares coding phases within grounded theory traditions. Thematic, content, narrative and discourse analysis each have their own analytic procedures.'}</p>
    <div class="qa-table-wrap"><table class="qa-coding-table qa-terminology-table">
      <caption>{language === 'zh' ? '紮根理論的編碼術語：Chun Tie、Birks與Francis（2019），表1' : 'Grounded theory coding terminology: Chun Tie, Birks and Francis (2019), Table 1'}</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">{language === 'zh' ? '紮根理論傳統' : 'Grounded theory tradition'}</th><th scope="col">{language === 'zh' ? '初始階段' : 'Initial phase'}</th><th scope="col">{language === 'zh' ? '中間階段' : 'Intermediate phase'}</th><th scope="col">{language === 'zh' ? '進階階段' : 'Advanced phase'}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">{language === 'zh' ? '傳統／經典' : 'Traditional / classic'}</th><td>{language === 'zh' ? '開放編碼' : 'Open coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '選擇編碼' : 'Selective coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '理論編碼' : 'Theoretical coding'}</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">{language === 'zh' ? '演進型（Strauss與Corbin）' : 'Evolved (Strauss and Corbin)'}</th><td>{language === 'zh' ? '開放編碼' : 'Open coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '主軸編碼' : 'Axial coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '選擇編碼' : 'Selective coding'}</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">{language === 'zh' ? '建構主義（Charmaz）' : 'Constructivist (Charmaz)'}</th><td>{language === 'zh' ? '初始編碼' : 'Initial coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '聚焦編碼' : 'Focused coding'}</td><td>{language === 'zh' ? '理論編碼' : 'Theoretical coding'}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <details class="qa-reveal"><summary>{language === 'zh' ? '為甚麼沒有統一名稱？' : 'Why do the names differ?'}</summary>
      <ul>
        <li>{language === 'zh' ? '發展脈絡：不同作者與學派逐步形成各自的術語及程序。' : 'History: authors and schools have developed distinct vocabularies and procedures.'}</li>
        <li>{language === 'zh' ? '知識觀：對理論如何從資料生成，以及研究者如何參與意義建構，各傳統有不同立場。' : 'Philosophical commitments: traditions differ in how they understand theory generation and the researcher’s role in constructing meaning.'}</li>
        <li>{language === 'zh' ? '分析任務：建立初始標籤、選取重要代碼、連結類別與整合理論，是不同的分析工作；術語須連同實際做法理解。' : 'Analytic tasks: labelling material, selecting significant codes, relating categories and integrating theory involve different work. Read each term alongside the procedure it names.'}</li>
      </ul>
      <p>{language === 'zh' ? '表格欄位方便比較，各術語的具體功能仍須依所選傳統理解。同名術語在不同傳統中的用法也可能有差異。' : 'The columns help comparison; each term’s specific function still depends on the chosen tradition. Even a shared name can have different uses across traditions.'}</p>
    </details>
    <p>{language === 'zh' ? '編碼階段、軟件中的父子代碼層級，以及「代碼→類別→主題」的組織方式，各有不同含義。主題分析的六階段亦不代表六層代碼。報告分析時，說明所採方法、術語定義及實際操作。' : 'Coding phases, parent–child code hierarchies in software, and code–category–theme groupings describe different aspects of analysis. The six phases of thematic analysis do not imply six code levels. Report your method, define your terms and explain what you actually did.'}</p>
    <p class="qa-teacher">{language === 'zh' ? '問AI：「以同一段訪談示範聚焦編碼與主軸編碼。說明各自的分析目的、所屬傳統及依據。」再用方法原文核對答案。' : 'Ask AI: “Illustrate focused and axial coding using the same interview extract. Explain each procedure’s purpose, tradition and methodological source.” Check its answer against the original methods texts.'}</p>
    <p class="qa-source"><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6318722/#section10-2050312118822927" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chun Tie, Birks &amp; Francis (2019) · Table 1 ↗</a> · <a href="https://doi.org/10.1191/1478088706qp063oa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Braun &amp; Clarke (2006) ↗</a></p>
  </div>)}
</div></section>}
